Lexifina's own contributions (the arrangement of the history, the commit messages, the tables, STRUCTURE.md,
REPRODUCE.md and the tools) are dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0 Universal:
https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/

The legal text is Tunisian legislation and is not Lexifina's. Each source's own terms:

1. Journal Officiel de la République Tunisienne (JORT), full text of the laws, decree-laws and decrees and the
   French translation, as the Imprimerie Officielle de la République Tunisienne (IORT) gives them on its text
   search, http://www.iort.gov.tn (folders lois/, decrets-lois/, decrets/). The site's footer reads "جميع الحقوق
   محفوظة المطبعة الرسمية للجمهورية التونسية" (all rights reserved, IORT); the site has no other terms of use and no
   robots.txt. The legal texts themselves are outside copyright (see below).

2. The codes in force, in the IORT's consolidated French editions published on legislation.tn, the national legal
   information portal (http://www.legislation.tn/fr/recherche/codes-en-vigueur), read from Internet Archive captures
   while the portal was unavailable (folder codes/). The IORT marks its editions "Tous droits réservés".

3. Loi n° 94-36 du 24 février 1994, relative à la propriété littéraire et artistique, as amended by Loi n° 2009-33
   du 23 juin 2009, consolidated copy hosted by legislation-securite.tn
   (https://legislation-securite.tn/wp-content/uploads/sites/5/2023/11/Loi-n°-94-36-du-24-Fevrier-1994-Fr.pdf),
   folder lois/1994/036-propriete-litteraire-et-artistique/. The site gives no licence for the text.

Official legislative texts are outside copyright in Tunisia. Article premier of Law 94-36, as amended by Law
2009-33:

  "La protection au titre du droit d'auteur s'étend aux expressions et ne couvre pas :
   [...] les textes officiels d'ordre législatif, administratif ou judiciaire et leurs traductions officielles."

Those hosts and the Tunisian authorities do not endorse this repository.

Changes made by Lexifina: page headers, footers and footnote markers of the code editions were removed and wrapped
lines joined; the JORT texts were cut into one Markdown file per article (preamble and closing in their own files);
the text was arranged as git commits. No word of law was written or corrected by Lexifina.
